 "relevance_note": "Tables II and III list two patients with heterozygous TNFAIP3 variants, e.g. '| S027 | TNFAIP3 | c.1127delC, p.S376fs'.",
 "method_note": "Read the whole paper manually; values were typed into a short Python script that only assembles the JSON (no automatic table transcription), then every span was checked by script against the paper. SCOPE: this is a multi-gene cohort (123 FOXP3-negative IPEX-like patients, 48 with genetic diagnoses in 27 genes). Only the two patients with TNFAIP3 variants (S027 and S087, Tables II and III) were extracted; the other 46 genetically diagnosed patients carry variants in other genes and the 75 undiagnosed patients have no individual data, so they were left out as outside the HA20 scope. AGE: Table II has an unlabelled 'Age' column; other rows (S045 Age '14 y' but 'Died age 16y'; S182 Age '4 m' but 'Died age 4y') show it is not age at last follow-up, and the text speaks of 'age at referral', so it is probably age at referral. It was recorded in age_at_last_evaluation as the only age given; treat with caution. is_proband=true rests on the cohort statement 'only probands were available for initial analysis'. n_patients_reported=2 is counted from the Table II/III rows; the text never states the TNFAIP3 count. VARIANTS: variant class taken from the authors' own notation ('p.S376fs', 'LoF', 'Truncating mutation' for S027; amino-acid substitution 'p.C767Y' for S087, which the authors never call missense in words). Genome build from the Table III column header 'hg19 position'. Pathogenicity from the 'This study' column, expanded with the table legend. The Table III 'Functional consequence; evidence for causality' cells give conservation and literature rationale, not assay results, so functional_evidence_statement is 'not reported'. Table II 'Inh' = 'AD' is the inheritance of the phenotype, not the variant's origin, so inheritance is 'not reported'; no parental testing is reported for these two. PHENOTYPES: S087's only clinical feature is the referral label '“IPEX”' (Table I treats '“IPEX” only' as a category); it was recorded as one feature row and no checklist item was inferred from it. For S027, eczema was mapped to skin lesions, failure to thrive to growth failure, thyroid autoantibodies to autoantibodies, and 'without frank thyroiditis' to autoimmune thyroiditis = excluded. CONTRADICTIONS (none affect the TNFAIP3 rows): text says '56 different variants' and also 'Of the 58 reported variants'; the MYO5B patient is 'SDH' in Table II but 'SBDH' in Table III; S045's cancer is 'intestinal adenocarcinoma' in Table II but 'gastric adenocarcinoma' in the text.",
